      "writtenOn": "2026-04-02T15:23:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t have much background on this code, but I\u0027m confused. It seems like this is meant to be a string value, not a boolean value (that is, \"this is the host\" not \"is there a host\"). Given that, it doesn\u0027t make sense to me to give a special meaning to the string \"false\". Is this a typical way these flags are \"unset\"?",
      "revId": "5332f27b3800c1e2b82b5c23903b599c3387f4d5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
